  "notes": [
    "Reflexive -ER verb based on *caer*. Uses reflexive pronouns (me/te/se/nos/se) in all tenses.",
    "Irregular yo presente: *me caigo* (not *caeo*). All other present forms are regular.",
    "Preterite: i→y in 3rd person (*se cayó*, *se cayeron*); accents on 1st and 2nd person (*me caí*, *te caíste*, *nos caímos*).",
    "Accented past participle: ***caído*** (the accent prevents the i from merging with the diphthong).",
    "Imperfect, future and conditional follow regular -ER patterns (but keep the accent where needed).",
    "*Me caí por las escaleras.* (I fell down the stairs.)",
    "*Se me cayó el móvil al suelo.* (My phone fell to the floor / I dropped my phone.)",
    "*Ten cuidado de no caerte.* (Be careful not to fall.)",
    "Related: *caer* (to fall — non-reflexive/transitive), *la caída* (fall), *caído/a* (fallen)"
  ],
